{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>And when men strive.</b> These men are Hebrews, for they are striving, striking one another, and so it is written: \"Why do you strike your fellow?\" (above, 2:13)." "<b>And they hurt.</b> It includes both of them, for sometimes the meaning is this one or that one, and likewise \"they shall burn him and them with fire\" (Leviticus 20)—this one or that one. And if both are Israelites, they have one law, and this woman is an Israelite woman." "<b>And there is no mishap.</b> To the woman." "<b>He shall be surely fined.</b> On account of the children that came out and died." "<b>As the husband of the woman shall lay upon him.</b> The father of the children, if the one who hurt acts willingly; and if not, he shall pay by order of the court, like \"and they shall judge before Elohim\" (1 Samuel 2:25)."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:37:03.902842708Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}